 test", "observed_hypothesis": "A specific opponent play type on the preceding possession suppresses each star's next-possession PPP relative to that star's baseline.", "observed_result": "PUTBACK is top suppressor for 6+ stars (e.g. D. Mitchell 1.178 to 0.884, d=-0.294, n_after=95; B. Beal d=-0.345 n=32; C. Holmgren d=-0.222 n=52). Other tops: TRANSITION (A. Davis -0.058), POST_UP (N. Jokic -0.075), PULL_ [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No multiplicity correction; n_after is 32-95 for several PUTBACK cells vs thousands of baseline possessions.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars; min n_after=30", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-022", "label": "Study family SF-APPM-022: Superstar suppression profiles (incl. Q5c sequential triggering)", "score": 0.789, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPM-022 (0.79)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Superstar suppression profiles (incl. Q5c sequential triggering)", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Specific opposing lineups, defenders, play types and preceding opponent play types suppress star efficiency.", "observed_result": "Q5c verdict 'rank-1 suppressor varies meaningfully across players'; e.g. Jokic after opp POST_UP 1.1271 (-0.0675, SE +/-0.0500, n=480); Curry forced POST_UP -0.209.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Rank-1 deltas mostly within 1-2 SE with no multiple-comparison control; OTHER artifact flagged in doc.", "observed_sample_and_power": "SE per cell reported", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "inconclusive", "observed_failure_type": "E_uncl